Z||000003||GT Bastard||04-29-2001||01:53 PM||||Well well well.... First off, lemme say that the car is being torn down for a new motor this comming weekend.  Reason being:  Bearings rattle, rings are shot(blows black smoke at WOT.)  On my way to the track I was hoping for 15's, but figured I'd run 16's due to the condition of the motor.  I learned A LOT!  Weather was about 80 degrees and humid with high winds so bad that some people were going home.  Anyhow, My first run was against a '97 SS Camaro with all the SLP stuff including headers!  Believe it or not, we were almost dead even up until 1/2 mile mark he started to pull away pretty steadily.  He ran a 15.2 to my 16.3!  Crappy!  Everybody was apparently running slower... There was a heavily modded LS1 6-speed with slicks and skinnies running only a 13.8!  My best run was a 15.9@85mph  I was pretty happy with this considering the amount of oil that my car is burning(it's easily visible on video.)  I'll have a video of the Fiero vs. '97 SS here pretty soon.  I was launching really hard and beating a lot of people out of the hole, but the Fiero just didn't have the top end.  One thing that is also inhibiting me to a certain degree is the 4.10 tranny.  The problem is that I'm forced to shift into 4th gear about 60ft before the end of the strip.  This sucks because the car falls on is a$$ when I hit 4th.  I'm seriously considering going back to the 3.65 tranny.  I also learned that the car runs about 4mph faster if I hold second all the way to 6,000 rpm because when I didn't it wouldn't accelerate hard enough into 3rd.  Anyhow, I was pretty happy with my times considering the circumstances. I'll try to get a video or two to post later on... see yaz!<P>oh yeah, the guy on the PA system once said, "Here's the Fiero again... In spanish, that means little foreign-looking car."  hehe..||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||04-29-2001||03:42 PM||||15.9 isn't bad at all considering the circumstances.  <P>Lucky your getting a new motor!  Keep that 2.8 up at 6 grand for long and you'll have a thrown rod hehe.  I want to see this footage, I've only seen one or two videos of Fiero's at the track... <P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||14
